WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.902
There's one number that tells you whether your AI feature is safe to ship. It is not accuracy. Accuracy hides the failures that actually hurt you.

00:08.902 --> 00:18.736
It's the failure rate on the cases that matter — the customer-facing, high-stakes ones. Not how often it's right, but how often it's wrong in a way that costs you.

00:18.736 --> 00:30.661
A feature can be ninety-five percent accurate and still be unshippable, if the five percent it gets wrong are refunds, medical advice, or legal claims. So I measure the failures that matter, not the average.

00:30.661 --> 00:34.969
Ship when that number is low enough to sleep at night. Not a moment before.

00:34.969 --> 00:37.273
Know your real number. Let's talk.

